&lt;h3&gt;About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the system software organisation that turns complex hardware platforms into reliable Graphcore systems.&amp;nbsp;As Director of System Software, you will report to the VP of Software and turn software strategy into clear priorities, plans and outcomes. You will lead the teams delivering firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and system software QA.&amp;nbsp;Your work will shape platform bring-up, production release and long-term support across Graphcore systems. You will align technical decisions with business priorities, delivery milestones and product readiness.&amp;nbsp;You will build a strong engineering organisation, developing managers, technical leaders and engineers. You will own execution, quality and cross-functional delivery across hardware, silicon, software and product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a leader who can think big, act fast and take responsibility for complex system outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;System Software works close to the hardware, where small decisions can shape product reliability at scale. The team operates through clear ownership, evidence-based planning and direct technical debate.&amp;nbsp;You will lead managers and specialists across firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and QA. Decisions are made through engineering judgement, clear trade-offs and a strong focus on delivery impact.&amp;nbsp;You will be expected to speak up, challenge assumptions and help resolve issues across hardware and software boundaries. Pace matters, but so do maintainability, security and long term quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· A strong track record leading system software teams across closely coupled hardware and software programmes.&lt;br&gt;· Experience managing managers or multiple technical teams, with clear ownership of deliv

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explore how a next-generation AI architecture behaves from rack scale to data centre scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Systems Engineer, you will investigate a novel AI computing architecture under demanding real-world workloads. You will work on problems where answers aren&#39;t readily known, turning curiosity into measurable evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design experiments, benchmark representative AI workloads and explore how hardware components and software interact at scale. When behaviour is unexpected, you will turn this into new measurements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will help infrastructure engineers, architects and application specialists understand system behaviour, performance, scalability and reliability across the stack. You will also help develop tooling and automation to collect, analyse and visualise system metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be an AI expert. You will need strong judgement, curiosity and a clear preference for evidence over opinion. You will love this role if you are someone who takes initiative, questions assumptions and enjoys working in areas where the answers are not yet known.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The System QA team is distributed across multiple locations. We work hard to stay connected and collaborate closely. Our daily team meetings feel more like a virtual coffee break than a formal status update with space to share ideas, ask questions, discuss discoveries and solve problems together.&lt;/p&gt;
